PART 13 – Understanding Milestones
12. What is a GitHub Milestone?
A milestone is used to group issues and Pull Requests associated with a particular project goal or release.

Imagine your bakery application has three development phases.
Milestone	Objective
Version 1.0	Homepage and About page
Version 2.0	Login and Registration
Version 3.0	Payment Gateway


Each milestone can contain multiple issues and Pull Requests.
