PART 17 – Important GitHub Collaboration Commands
Command	Purpose
git clone URL	Clone a repository
git remote -v	View remote repositories
git remote add upstream URL	Add original repository
git fetch upstream	Fetch original repository changes
git switch -c feature	Create feature branch
git add .	Stage changes
git commit -m "message"	Commit changes
git push -u origin feature	Push feature branch
git pull	Fetch and integrate changes
git merge upstream/main	Merge original main branch
git rebase upstream/main	Rebase current branch onto upstream main


Remember that Pull Requests, Issues, labels and milestones are primarily managed through GitHub's interface or its APIs, not through these basic Git commands.

